1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,960
This is Elon Musk, the first trillionaire in human history.

2
00:00:04,620 --> 00:00:09,100
You probably think his new fight with India is just about a satellite internet licence.

3
00:00:09,840 --> 00:00:18,860
But in one single week of October 2026, that fight dragged in India's richest man, its opposition leader, and its government.

4
00:00:19,260 --> 00:00:24,620
He accused unnamed oligarchs of committing a crime against the people of India.

5
00:00:25,610 --> 00:00:30,460
He mockingly called Mukesh Ambani the Prime Minister of India.

6
00:00:31,240 --> 00:00:37,240
And when Rahul Gandhi joined in, the richest man on Earth publicly thanked him.

7
00:00:37,720 --> 00:00:43,900
The government called his claims baseless, and a former minister warned that satellites come with serious security risks.

8
00:00:44,640 --> 00:00:50,800
At the very same time, police in Delhi were detaining young protesters who say India's voter lists are being manipulated.

9
00:00:50,800 --> 00:00:58,020
So the question millions of Indians are now asking is simple, is Elon Musk meddling in Indian politics?

10
00:00:59,080 --> 00:01:02,740
It isn't only about Starlink, and it isn't only about Ambani.

11
00:01:03,280 --> 00:01:09,500
It's about power, and who gets to control how one point four billion people connect to the world.

12
00:01:10,040 --> 00:01:16,860
Now, let's take a closer look at the story of the trillionaire, the tycoon, and the fight for India's sky.

13
00:01:16,860 --> 00:01:25,040
Starlink is a network of thousands of satellites flying low around the Earth, beaming internet down to a small dish on your roof.

14
00:01:25,820 --> 00:01:31,480
It works in deserts, mountains and villages where no cable or mobile tower has ever reached.

15
00:01:32,200 --> 00:01:38,380
And India, with hundreds of millions of people still offline, looked like the biggest prize of all.

16
00:01:39,080 --> 00:01:46,360
In 2021, Starlink started taking pre-orders in India, and more than five thousand people paid a ninety-nine dollar deposit.

17
00:01:46,760 --> 00:01:50,820
There was just one small problem, it didn't have a licence.

18
00:01:51,580 --> 00:01:58,580
The government told people not to subscribe, Starlink had to refund everyone, and its India head stepped down soon after.

19
00:01:59,060 --> 00:02:06,380
Then came the real battle, over something you can't even see, the radio spectrum that satellites use to talk to the ground.

20
00:02:07,080 --> 00:02:12,000
Ambani's Reliance Jio wanted that spectrum sold in an auction, where the biggest bidders win.

21
00:02:12,120 --> 00:02:19,100
Musk called that unprecedented, and in late 2024, the government sided with him and chose to allocate it instead.

22
00:02:19,660 --> 00:02:21,280
And then, the twist.

23
00:02:22,160 --> 00:02:31,960
In March 2025, Jio and Airtel, the two companies that should have feared Starlink most, signed deals to sell Starlink to their own customers.

24
00:02:32,440 --> 00:02:40,160
By the middle of 2025, Starlink had its licence and its space regulator's approval, and it looked like the door was finally open.

25
00:02:40,460 --> 00:02:42,620
But the door never fully opened.

26
00:02:42,920 --> 00:02:53,560
Starlink, Jio's satellite arm and the Airtel backed OneWeb all still needed spectrum and a final security clearance, and month after month, nothing moved.

27
00:02:54,340 --> 00:03:01,040
So in October 2026, Elon Musk did what he always does when he loses patience, he went to X.

28
00:03:01,340 --> 00:03:10,260
On October seventh, Musk wrote that Starlink was being blocked by certain oligarchs, to protect what he called their monopolistic chokehold on the Indian people.

29
00:03:10,780 --> 00:03:14,120
He didn't name anyone, but he said you can guess who they are.

30
00:03:15,060 --> 00:03:18,060
And he called it a crime against the people of India.

31
00:03:18,760 --> 00:03:24,800
The next day, India's communications ministry hit back, calling the claim baseless and misconceived.

32
00:03:25,400 --> 00:03:32,540
It said all three satellite companies were at broadly the same regulatory stage, and that security checks had to come first.

33
00:03:33,200 --> 00:03:39,920
Musk answered with a question that exploded across Indian social media, is Ambani the real boss of India?

34
00:03:40,640 --> 00:03:42,500
Then the opposition walked in.

35
00:03:43,240 --> 00:03:54,700
Rahul Gandhi, India's Leader of the Opposition, welcomed Musk to India and told him to wait until he discovered the other guy, a line many read as a jab at another tycoon, Gautam Adani.

36
00:03:55,360 --> 00:03:58,700
Musk thanked him, and called the situation indeed troubling.

37
00:03:59,140 --> 00:04:05,480
Former minister Rajeev Chandrasekhar, from the ruling B J P, fired back that patience was a necessity.

38
00:04:06,380 --> 00:04:13,260
He warned that satellite internet carries serious security risks in a country that has faced years of terror and insurgency.

39
00:04:14,240 --> 00:04:17,500
And he mocked Rahul Gandhi as Musk's latest fan.

40
00:04:18,320 --> 00:04:21,060
On October ninth, Musk went even further.

41
00:04:21,580 --> 00:04:33,840
In a post addressed to Dear Prime Minister Ambani, he apologized for not realizing that Ambani was the real boss of India, and asked if he would please allow Starlink to compete.

42
00:04:34,720 --> 00:04:41,720
Communications minister Jyotiraditya Scindia answered that India does not allow a monopoly in any sector.

43
00:04:42,260 --> 00:04:51,220
By October eleventh, Musk was promising an affordable Starlink, and saying Ambani's profits would be lower, but he wouldn't go out of business.

44
00:04:51,960 --> 00:04:54,860
To some Indians, he looked like a hero taking on a giant.

45
00:04:55,460 --> 00:05:00,460
To others, he looked like a foreign billionaire trying to bully an elected government in public.

46
00:05:01,080 --> 00:05:03,800
Now, you're probably thinking the answer is obvious.

47
00:05:04,140 --> 00:05:11,940
Ambani owns Jio, Jio wants to launch its own satellite internet, and no business wants a rival as powerful as Musk.

48
00:05:12,420 --> 00:05:19,620
And to understand why that idea feels so believable to so many Indians, you have to know how the Ambanis built their empire.

49
00:05:20,340 --> 00:05:29,280
Enter Dhirubhai Ambani, a schoolteacher's son from Gujarat who reportedly started out as a petrol station attendant in Aden, in Yemen.

50
00:05:29,900 --> 00:05:35,520
In 1958, he came back to Bombay and started trading yarn and spices with very little money.

51
00:05:36,160 --> 00:05:40,780
Within a few decades, Reliance had become one of the biggest companies in India.

52
00:05:41,360 --> 00:05:46,840
This was the era of the licence raj, when you needed government permission for almost everything.

53
00:05:47,360 --> 00:05:58,500
Critics, and a famous biography called The Polyester Prince, claimed Reliance was unusually good at getting rules bent in its favour, claims the Ambanis always disputed.

54
00:05:58,840 --> 00:06:05,960
That book was never officially released in India after legal threats, but the reputation it described never fully went away.

55
00:06:06,460 --> 00:06:11,720
Then, in 2016, his son Mukesh did something nobody had seen before.

56
00:06:12,480 --> 00:06:17,500
He launched Jio and gave away calls and mobile data for free, for months.

57
00:06:18,070 --> 00:06:26,960
By the company's own count, Jio reached a hundred million users in about a hundred and seventy days, one of the fastest growth stories in business history.

58
00:06:27,740 --> 00:06:31,840
Rivals bled money, and the market shrank to a handful of survivors.

59
00:06:32,360 --> 00:06:41,740
Before Jio, around a dozen mobile companies fought for Indian customers, and today Jio and Airtel together control more than eighty percent of the market.

60
00:06:42,340 --> 00:06:48,860
Airtel accused Jio of predatory pricing, but India's competition regulator rejected that complaint in 2017.

61
00:06:49,740 --> 00:06:51,800
Here's the part both sides agree on.

62
00:06:52,440 --> 00:07:02,900
A gigabyte of mobile data cost Indians around two hundred and seventy rupees in 2014, and by 2020 it cost about eleven, which brought hundreds of millions of people online.

63
00:07:03,640 --> 00:07:12,840
But in 2024, with only a few players left, Jio raised its prices by up to twenty-seven percent, and its rivals followed within days.

64
00:07:13,380 --> 00:07:24,520
Now Jio reportedly wants the sky too, with plans for a satellite network of its own, and on October twenty-first, it's expected to open India's biggest stock market listing ever.

65
00:07:25,220 --> 00:07:27,620
Remember that date, because it matters more than it looks.

66
00:07:28,240 --> 00:07:33,600
So yes, Ambani has a lot to lose, but if you only look at Ambani, you miss the bigger picture.

67
00:07:34,160 --> 00:07:37,600
To see that picture, look at what Musk has done in other countries.

68
00:07:38,180 --> 00:07:47,320
In 2022, he bought Twitter for forty-four billion dollars, renamed it X, and became the owner of one of the most powerful political megaphones on the planet.

69
00:07:47,940 --> 00:07:54,320
He called himself a free speech absolutist, and he started using that megaphone himself, every single day.

70
00:07:54,820 --> 00:07:58,380
In America's 2024 election, Musk didn't just post.

71
00:07:58,840 --> 00:08:11,340
According to federal election filings, he spent more than two hundred and ninety million dollars backing Donald Trump and other Republicans, including a giveaway of a million dollars a day to swing state voters who signed his petition.

72
00:08:12,020 --> 00:08:19,500
After Trump won, Musk was handed a government cost-cutting team, and within months, the two men had a very public falling out.

73
00:08:20,060 --> 00:08:26,680
In Brazil, he refused court orders to block certain accounts, and called a Supreme Court judge a dictator.

74
00:08:27,400 --> 00:08:34,260
In 2024, Brazil switched off X across the entire country for more than a month, until the company backed down.

75
00:08:34,680 --> 00:08:39,320
It was a foreign businessman against a nation's highest court, and the court won.

76
00:08:40,020 --> 00:08:48,560
In Germany, he openly backed the far-right Alternative for Germany party before the 2025 election, and even spoke by video to one of its rallies.

77
00:08:49,260 --> 00:08:57,600
In Britain, he called for Parliament to be dissolved, and told an anti-immigration rally that violence was coming, and that they had to fight back or die.

78
00:08:58,560 --> 00:09:01,520
Politicians across Britain condemned those words as dangerous.

79
00:09:02,000 --> 00:09:03,880
And then there's the switch.

80
00:09:03,880 --> 00:09:15,020
In 2022, during the war in Ukraine, Musk refused a request to turn on Starlink near Crimea, a request he said would have been used to attack the Russian fleet.

81
00:09:15,860 --> 00:09:21,860
Think about how strange that is, a private businessman holding a switch that could shape a war.

82
00:09:22,620 --> 00:09:23,820
So here's the pattern.

83
00:09:24,880 --> 00:09:33,760
Musk picks a side in another country's political fight, posts about it to more than two hundred million followers, and dares the government to respond.

84
00:09:34,620 --> 00:09:42,080
His fans call it fighting censorship, and his critics call it a billionaire meddling in democracies that never voted for him.

85
00:09:42,520 --> 00:09:44,520
With India, it started as a friendship.

86
00:09:45,080 --> 00:09:55,700
In 2015, Narendra Modi visited Tesla's factory in California, and in 2023, after meeting him again in New York, Musk said he was a fan of Modi.

87
00:09:56,320 --> 00:09:59,820
He promised that Tesla would come to India as soon as humanly possible.

88
00:09:59,820 --> 00:10:01,340
Then the cracks appeared.

89
00:10:01,860 --> 00:10:11,080
X took the Indian government to court over its content blocking orders, saying it had already obeyed ninety-one percent of more than twenty-nine thousand takedown requests.

90
00:10:11,580 --> 00:10:16,680
In 2025, the Karnataka High Court ruled against X, and the company appealed.

91
00:10:17,220 --> 00:10:25,960
That same year, X's chatbot, Grok, started answering Indian users in Hindi slang, and making cheeky comments about Modi and Rahul Gandhi.

92
00:10:26,600 --> 00:10:29,980
India's technology ministry said it was talking to X about it.

93
00:10:30,320 --> 00:10:36,180
It looked like a joke, but it was a reminder that Musk's machines were now part of India's political conversation.

94
00:10:36,900 --> 00:10:46,180
Back in 2024, security forces in Manipur had seized Starlink equipment alongside weapons, even though Musk says Starlink's beams are switched off over India.

95
00:10:46,860 --> 00:10:54,420
And in May 2026, after years of arguing over import taxes, Tesla officially dropped its plan to build a factory in India.

96
00:10:55,020 --> 00:11:00,400
So by the time Musk called Ambani the real boss of India, the friendship had already gone cold.

97
00:11:00,840 --> 00:11:03,160
Now look at what's happening inside India right now.

98
00:11:03,940 --> 00:11:14,960
In May 2026, India's Chief Justice made a remark that seemed to compare some activists and unemployed young people to cockroaches, which he later said was about people with fake degrees.

99
00:11:15,660 --> 00:11:22,060
The very next day, a young activist named Abhijeet Dipke launched a satirical movement called the Cockroach Janta Party.

100
00:11:22,580 --> 00:11:30,560
It began as a joke, but it caught the anger of millions of young Indians about jobs, prices and who really runs the country.

101
00:11:31,120 --> 00:11:37,100
Then it found a bigger target, a nationwide revision of voter lists that removed millions of names.

102
00:11:37,760 --> 00:11:46,580
The Election Commission says it's removing dead and duplicate voters, but the movement says it's choosing who gets to vote, and wants the Chief Election Commissioner to resign.

103
00:11:47,100 --> 00:11:48,780
Rahul Gandhi joined that demand.

104
00:11:49,420 --> 00:11:56,380
And on October tenth, the very same week as Musk's posts, the movement called people to Jantar Mantar in Delhi.

105
00:11:57,080 --> 00:12:06,140
Police reportedly put more than sixty thousand security personnel on the streets, and detained the movement's three leaders from inside their plane after it landed.

106
00:12:06,820 --> 00:12:17,840
Reports said opposition leaders including Arvind Kejriwal and Mamata Banerjee were also detained, and a popular YouTuber was reportedly placed under house arrest.

107
00:12:18,420 --> 00:12:24,620
The ruling B J P called the protest a flop show, and police said the protest site itself stayed clear.

108
00:12:25,420 --> 00:12:31,160
The protesters say they were silenced, the government says it kept order, and the movement has promised to keep going.

109
00:12:31,760 --> 00:12:33,860
Now put the two stories side by side.

110
00:12:34,260 --> 00:12:41,800
On one side, a young, angry country, with an opposition leader attacking the government over elections and big business.

111
00:12:42,500 --> 00:12:50,720
On the other side, a trillionaire with a global megaphone, attacking the same government over the same tycoons, in the very same week.

112
00:12:51,480 --> 00:12:55,580
To be clear, there's no public evidence that Musk has said a word about these protests.

113
00:12:56,620 --> 00:13:05,000
But critics in India warn that this is exactly the kind of moment an outsider with a huge platform can use, when a country is already divided.

114
00:13:05,640 --> 00:13:12,520
One post, amplified to hundreds of millions of people, can pour fuel on a fire that's already burning.

115
00:13:13,060 --> 00:13:15,380
Musk's supporters see it very differently.

116
00:13:15,860 --> 00:13:23,640
They say he's a businessman who waited five years, and simply said out loud what many Indians already suspect about crony capitalism.

117
00:13:24,300 --> 00:13:27,340
So is he a whistleblower, or is he a player?

118
00:13:27,940 --> 00:13:37,360
In June 2026, SpaceX went public at a value of about one point eight trillion dollars, and Musk became the first trillionaire in history.

119
00:13:38,160 --> 00:13:44,040
He owns the rockets, the satellites, the social network, and an artificial intelligence company.

120
00:13:44,740 --> 00:13:49,680
No private citizen has ever controlled this many of the pipes that information flows through.

121
00:13:50,280 --> 00:13:56,560
And for someone who already has everything money can buy, many analysts argue that what's left is influence.

122
00:13:57,440 --> 00:13:58,760
Remember the switch over Crimea.

123
00:13:59,540 --> 00:14:05,940
Now imagine that same kind of switch over a country where hundreds of millions of people could one day get their internet from the sky.

124
00:14:06,540 --> 00:14:10,280
That's why India's government keeps repeating one word, security.

125
00:14:10,560 --> 00:14:20,540
At least four in ten Indians are still not online, the last giant internet market left on Earth, and whoever connects them could shape what they see, read and believe.

126
00:14:21,120 --> 00:14:28,880
And remember October twenty-first, the day Ambani's Jio is expected to hit the stock market, because Musk's attacks landed just days before it.

127
00:14:29,440 --> 00:14:30,700
So that's the story.

128
00:14:31,260 --> 00:14:44,060
Not just a delayed licence, but a five-year fight over the sky, a tycoon who rewrote India's telecom market, and a trillionaire who has stepped into politics from America to Brazil, Germany and Britain.

129
00:14:44,700 --> 00:14:49,740
And now, in a tense week for Indian democracy, his posts landed right in the middle of it.

130
00:14:50,040 --> 00:14:57,400
Starlink could bring the internet to villages that have waited decades for it, and more competition could push prices down for everyone.

131
00:14:57,840 --> 00:15:02,500
But a country also has to ask who it's letting in, and what they want in return.

132
00:15:03,360 --> 00:15:09,780
So what do you think, is Elon Musk meddling in Indian politics, or is he just a businessman who ran out of patience?

133
00:15:10,440 --> 00:15:14,360
Tell me in the comments, and keep it respectful, because both sides have a point.

134
00:15:14,920 --> 00:15:20,760
If you want the full story behind the headlines, the long version and not the clip, this channel is for you.

135
00:15:21,220 --> 00:15:22,740
Subscribe for the next long story.

